WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
One morning, a fox walks
across a school field.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.430
Two people write about it.

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.230
One writes a news
report, with a headline.

4
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.670
The other writes a diary entry.

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.250
"I couldn't believe my eyes!

6
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.270
" Same fox.

7
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.370
Same field.

8
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.730
Same morning.

9
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.690
So why do the two texts
feel so different?

10
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.930
And how could you compare them fairly?

11
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.590
In this mission, you'll learn
three ways to describe how a text

12
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.200
works.

13
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.260
You'll spot the features
each text type uses.

14
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:33.330
You'll compare two texts
with words like whereas.

15
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.950
And you'll put your
reading skills together.

16
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.030
Your mission: explain why one
event can make two very different

17
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.210
texts.
